Package: InterPlotComp
Title: Inter-Plot Competition Analysis for Plant Breeding Trials
Version: 3.8.1
Authors@R:
    person("Tolera", "Keno", email = "tolekeno@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Fits direct-competition mixed models to unbordered single-row-plot
    breeding trials using 'ASReml-R' as the computational engine. For every
    genotype the model separates the effect expressed in its own plot from the
    effect it imposes on neighbouring plots, and combines them into the value
    the genotype would express in a pure stand. Handles a single trial or a
    series of environments, separable AR1 x AR1 spatial residuals, pedigree and
    genomic relationship matrices, exact prediction error variances, and
    publication-quality figure export. Includes a 'Shiny' interface, launched
    with run_app(). 'ASReml-R' is commercial software licensed by VSNi and is
    not supplied by this package; it must be installed and licensed separately.
    Methods follow Stringer, Cullis and Thompson (2011, Journal of
    Agricultural, Biological, and Environmental Statistics 16:269-281) and
    Hunt, Smith, Jordan and Cullis (2013) <doi:10.1007/s13253-012-0117-7>.
